# Intent: the unit stays usable and reachable when the hub is not (owner decision 2026-10-23: "even with no hub or Wi-Fi the unit must keep responding"). (1) Wi-Fi power save is NONE while the websocket is down (serial log 2026-10-23: the unit joined the mesh AP but its SYN never got an answer and the Studio could not even ping it, right after "Setting WiFi power save level: LOW_POWER (MAX_MODEM)", listen interval 10 beacons); with the hub up an idle unit uses MIN_MODEM instead of MAX_MODEM; PERFORMANCE while speaking is unchanged. (2) A tap or the wake word no longer blocks the main task: OpenAudioChannel waited up to 10 s for the persistent socket ("main loop stalled", the screen and touch froze); it now waits 400 ms and the caller shows a calm "Can't reach Home" bubble, a doubtful face and a short tone for three seconds, logs an offline_tap event and goes back to idle. (3) The reconnect task caps its backoff at 30 s, logs every attempt (attempt, duration, error code, next retry) and pushes a "wifi" event {state ws_up|ws_down|ws_retry, wifi, rssi, attempt, error, next_ms, took_ms} for the host log. (4) After 10 s without the hub the ring shows a dim steady amber and the speech bubble says "Offline"; both clear when the socket is back (the screen-sleep blanking still wins).
# Upstream: 78/xiaozhi-esp32 main/protocols/websocket_protocol.cc and main/application.cc (MIT); m5stack/StackChan firmware/main/hal/board/stackchan.cc, hal_bridge.h, hal/hal_io_expander.cpp (MIT). Applies after 074.
# Check after a flash: with the hub stopped, tap the screen and say the wake word: "Can't reach Home" with a short tone appears within a second and the screen never freezes (no "main loop stalled" in the log); after ten seconds the ring is dim amber and the bubble says Offline; the host log shows "unit wifi:" lines with the attempt and error; start the hub: the ring and bubble clear and the unit connects; ping the unit from another computer while the hub is down: it answers.
